NNAAMMEE
     symedit - GUI symbol editor for the vellum library

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssyymmeeddiitt [_o_p_t_i_o_n_s] [_l_i_b_r_a_r_y]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ssyymmeeddiitt edits a vveelllluumm symbol library file: draw a part once
     here - a lab instrument, a relay, a connector - and place it
     in every schematic afterwards.  The optional _l_i_b_r_a_r_y argu-
     ment names the file to edit (the Edit button in vveelllluumm pas-
     ses the current library); the default is the user scratch
     library, /usr/vellum/etc/symbols.  The status line shows the
     file's name in brackets.  It must be run under the zzvviieeww
     desktop; see zzvviieeww.

     The canvas shows one symbol magnified, dotted at every
     quarter grid unit with heavier marks on whole grid units.
     The cross is the ORIGIN: the point vveelllluumm places, rotates
     and mirrors the symbol around.  Under the tool cells sits a
     true-scale preview - exactly what the palette and canvas of
     vveelllluumm will draw.

     The tools:

                  SSeeggdrag draws a segment, snapped to quarter units
                  CCiirrccdrag from the centre; radius in quarter units
                  AArrccdrag from the centre to the START point (radius
                            and start angle), then drag once more to sweep
                            out the end; angles snap to 5 degrees
                  PPiinnclick places a connection pin, snapped to WHOLE
                            grid units - pins are where wires snap in vveelllluumm.
                            A second click on a pin asks for its NAME, which
                            the netlist export prints (Q1.B instead of Q1.2),
                            and its TYPE - in, out, power or bidirectional -
                            which the B-checkR electrical rules test (two
                            outputs on a net conflict, an output must not
                            drive a power rail, all-input nets are undriven)
                  CChhaarrclick asks for one small-font character
                  MMoovveedrag an element to move it; a drag on empty
                            canvas marquee-selects, and the set then moves
                            as one and deletes with xx
                  DDeellclick removes the nearest element

     The rr and mm keys rotate (a quarter turn) and mirror the
     WHOLE symbol around the origin - draw one gate half, mirror
     it.  The ff key copies a symbol IN from another library file
     as the starting point (asks for the file and the code; the
     buffer is replaced, the code and prefix stay).  The ii key
     IMPORTS A DRAWING as the stencil (VELLUM.md sec. 55): it
     asks for the .dd file, the grid point that becomes the symbol
     origin (blank = the drawing's first NN marker) and the scale,
     then converts under exactly the rules vveellssyymm uses - lines,
     wires, boxes and polylines become segments, circles and arcs
     themselves, a ONE-CHARACTER text a glyph, and the NN markers


